tests: give the tensors of test-barrier defined data
Fold-into: upstream/ggml-cpu

Base: llama.cpp commit c6824a9 plus every patch of the series before this one.

test-barrier measures the barriers of the CPU thread pool. It builds graphs
of Q4_0 matrix products, but it does not write the matrices or the F32
input, thus the products read indeterminate memory, and the F16 scales can
be NaN or Inf. MemorySanitizer reports a use of an uninitialized value in
ggml_lookup_fp16_to_fp32, called by ggml_vec_dot_q4_0_q8_0.

The change: zero the data of each tensor of the context after the graphs
are built, before the first compute. Test code only.

diff --git a/tests/test-barrier.cpp b/tests/test-barrier.cpp
index 61f73ad..f123467 100644
--- a/tests/test-barrier.cpp
+++ b/tests/test-barrier.cpp
@@ -5,12 +5,21 @@
 #include <iostream>
 #include <cstdio>
 #include <cstdlib>
+#include <cstring>
 #include <cassert>
 #include <vector>
 #include <thread>
 
 #define MAX_NARGS 2
 
+// The test measures the barriers, not the values, but the matrix products still read their
+// inputs: give every tensor of the context defined data (zeros) before the first compute.
+static void zero_tensors(struct ggml_context * ctx) {
+    for (struct ggml_tensor * t = ggml_get_first_tensor(ctx); t != NULL; t = ggml_get_next_tensor(ctx, t)) {
+        memset(t->data, 0, ggml_nbytes(t));
+    }
+}
